From 90d793ca5c92b34218f61b0d056f814f4a7e2a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:51:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 006/139] feat(look): epic renderer, golden-hour light and
 textured arena under -MageArenaLook=epic

Look/EpicLook dresses the greybox after Build() only under the epic look: M_EpicSurface
(world-aligned triplanar stone, sand with grain and rake, flagstone, banner, plain tints) on
the shell and props by their greybox colour; the painted golden-hour panorama (M_EpicSky, a
sky material the real-time sky light captures) on a far dome; sky atmosphere for the light;
a low warm sun placed from the seat's forward with soft virtual shadows; volumetric haze;
the braziers as flickering lights; a point light per visible spell-glow colour layer; Lumen
GI and reflections, manual exposure, filmic curve, bloom and a mild warm/teal grade in an
unbound post volume; Brennic's epic material through BrennicEpicLook. Deferred shading,
distance fields, Lumen, VSM and TSR are start-up settings passed on the command line
(EpicLook::LaunchIniOverrides), so the project stays forward and flat and quest are
unchanged. -run=CreateEpicLookAssets builds the surfaces from the staged studio stills
(interim copies of Tier A's, to be replaced by their commits). capture-epic.ps1 takes a
game/key-art pair with the frame time (MAGEVR_EPIC_FRAME). MaterialGraph re-creates a
material over an existing package on a re-run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
