From 5865c5d53982db6e4b34f2dc8c8c1003b80429a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:37:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 018/139] feat(art): Brennic's arms-out Cast clip for the
 non-flat looks

cast_open.py takes the committed Cast take and, from the wind-up, blends both upper arms,
forearms and wrists toward S1's forward-and-out spread (palms toward the seat), blending back
over the last frames so the clip still hands off to Idle; same 47 frames. -run=
ImportBrennicCastOpen imports it as /Game/Look/Epic/Brennic/A_Brennic_CastOpen on the
committed SK_Brennic_Skeleton (animation only: mesh, rig and the four clips untouched).
RivalFigure plays it for Cast under the non-flat looks; flat keeps the committed Cast. Visual
only: clip lengths, hits and projectile targets come from the kernel, not the pose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
