From b826e925b5d6c595bb50538c5168b33cb56dd4fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:33:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 051/139] feat(look): deterministic S1 shot clock, gap-free
 ward arch, bigger rune flames

Shared (flat unchanged). From its settle on, the S1 shot holds the world's
game time (the materials' Time: ward pan, flame lick) and the presentation's
clock (QuestSpells::Clock: flipbook cells) at 12.5 s (-MageArenaS1ClockS=),
so every round shows the same animation phase: two runs differ by 0.11 of 255
on average. The ward's cards now stand upright edge to edge and M_Q_Ward lifts
the wave inside them along the arch curve, so the wedge gaps Tier B found at
the ribbon's base are gone, still one instanced draw. The Wardstones' rune
flames and halos are larger so the Tithe cap reads at distance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
