+++ b/docs/research/EPIC-LOOK-2026-10-28.md
@@ -0,0 +1,160 @@
+# Epic look: the record (graphics push, 2026-10-28)
+
+Tier B of `docs/concepts/GRAPHICS-PUSH-2026-10-28.md`: how close can this game get to key art S1 with anything the
+desktop renderer can do? Branch `push/epic-look`, behind `-MageArenaLook=epic`. Since `b9778e4` the branch also carries
+the quest look (Tier A's `push/quest-look` merged in), so it is the one branch with flat, quest and epic. Flat stays the
+greybox byte for byte: the suite held 345/348 every round (the three Lynx-only reds `Fire.Golden`, `Overlay.Golden`,
+`Rivals.NullPath`; `Sigils.Accuracy` failed twice on its 0.5 ms timing bar under two-builder load, accepted as noise).
+Blind judges: baseline 14.0; epic r2 24.0 (25/24/23); epic r6 27.0 (26/25/30), the best frame of round 2 (quest r7 24.0).
+Judges named the golden sky, the grade and the white-gold fireball heart; they marked down the pylon tops (fixed in
+`637dc21`), the opponent's size at 16 m (owner ruling: he stays at 16 m) and the debug-looking cuff (restyled).
+
+## 1. What it is, file by file
+
+All under `apps/vr/Game/Source/MageArenaVR/` unless a path says otherwise.
+
+**Renderer (epic only).** The project stays forward-shaded, so flat and quest are unchanged. An epic run passes its
+start-up settings on the command line (`EpicLook::LaunchIniOverrides`, used by `apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1` and
+`apps/vr/tools/capture-epic.ps1`): `r.ForwardShading=False`, `r.GenerateMeshDistanceFields=True`, Lumen GI and reflections,
+`r.Shadow.Virtual.Enable=1`, TSR. D3D12 at SM5 with 64-bit atomics on the RTX Spark N1X runs software Lumen and VSM.
+
+**`Look/EpicLook.*`**: `EpicLook::DressArena`, called from `AArenaGreybox::Build` in place of the box sky, and
+`AEpicLookRig`, the ticking actor that owns the runtime pieces.
+- Surfaces: every greybox part whose tint matches a layout colour gets an instance of `M_EpicSurface`
+  (`Look/EpicSurfaceHlsl.h`): world-aligned triplanar texture with a luminance bump, sand with grain and rake, the banner
+  on the cube face's own UV, plain tints for iron and wood. Textures: Tier A's staged studio stills (stone, sand,
+  flagstone, banner), imported by `-run=CreateEpicLookAssets` (`Tools/CreateEpicLookAssetsCommandlet.*`).
+- Sky: the painted panorama (Tier A's `sky-01`) on a 200 m sphere through `M_EpicSky`: looked up by view direction so
+  it sits at infinity, a sky material the real-time sky light captures, horizon lifted 11 degrees so its hills meet the
+  stands, a warm haze band. The physical sky atmosphere still lights the scene; on its own it rendered a grey-brown sky
+  at this sun height, which is why the painted dome is there.
+- Light: low warm sun placed from the seat's forward (azimuth -55, pitch 11, 2.2 degree source, virtual shadows), real-time
+  sky light, volumetric height fog, brazier and pylon fire point lights flickering on three waves, a point light per
+  visible spell-glow colour layer (the fire bolt lights the sand), a warm rim light on Brennic on lighting channel 1 only.
+- Post: an unbound volume. Lumen, manual exposure (-0.2 EV), filmic curve, bloom 0.9, vignette, and the colour-grading LUT
+  (section 4).
+- Spell extras over Tier A's shared VFX: `M_EpicFireHeart`, an additive HDR white-gold heart card on warm bolt cores
+  only; `M_EpicWard`, Tier A's arch ward graph plus refraction and a depth fade (default on;
+  `-MageArenaEpicNoWardRefract`); Tier A's licking fire and halo on the floor braziers and the four pylons
+  (`QuestLook::BuildPylons`).
+- `-MageArenaEpicShot=<dir>` (`capture-epic.ps1`): game and key-art stills after shaders and light settle, plus
+  `MAGEVR_EPIC_FRAME` (frame and GPU ms over 120 frames).
+
+**Shared hero assets (every non-flat look)**
+- `Look/BrennicEpicLook.*`, `Tools/CreateBrennicEpicCommandlet.*`, `Tools/ImportBrennicCastOpenCommandlet.*`: Brennic's
+  texture set and arms-out Cast (section 2).
+- `Look/PlayerHandsLook.*`, `Tools/CreatePlayerHandsCommandlet.*`: the skinned hands (section 2). Hook in
+  `Greybox/HandPresentationComponent.cpp`.
+- `Look/CrowdLook.*`, `Look/CrowdPaintedAtlas.h` (generated), `Tools/CreateCrowdPaintedCommandlet.*`: the painted crowd
+  and the stand banners (section 2). Hook in `Greybox/ArenaGreyboxActor.cpp`.
+- `Look/CuffLook.*`, `Tools/CreateCuffStyledCommandlet.*`: the wrist cuff's bronze-framed panel and flat rune-line bars;
+  the crowd placeholder band shows off flat only while it swells. Hooks in `Session/SessionPresentation.cpp`.
+- Coping on the wall off flat (instanced into the wall's own component) and the epic's wall-hung banners:
+  `Greybox/ArenaGreyboxActor.cpp`.
+- `Tools/MaterialGraph.h`: the commandlets' material-graph, texture import and save helpers; `NewMaterial` moves an
+  existing object aside on a re-run (without it a second run failed to save).
+
+## 2. The hero pipelines
+
+**Brennic** (`apps/vr/art/characters/brennic/epic/`, details in `../HANDOFF.md`). A texture-space finish of the committed
+DINOv3 bake (ad38b9b) on its own UVs, so `SK_Brennic`, its rig and its four clips are untouched.
+- `head_ortho.py`: front orthographic render of the head, for placing face landmarks.
+- `face_overlay.py`: the face drawn in that frame (eye whites, irises, lash lines, a heavy scowling brow, mouth line,
+  beard strands over a pale chin patch).
+- `bake_epic.py`: Cycles bakes of position, normal, AO and the albedo with the overlay projected along +X onto the
+  front-facing head. From those it builds region masks (tunic, skin, iron collar, bronze brooch, hair, leather, cloak),
+  then the regraded albedo, a DirectX normal from hair curls, wool weave and the albedo's own folds, and an ORM map
+  (R AO, G roughness, B metallic, A skin mask). The UV coverage is rasterised from the triangles.
+- `-run=CreateBrennicEpic` builds `M_BrennicEpic` with subsurface-profile skin through the mask.
+- `cast_open.py` and `-run=ImportBrennicCastOpen`: `A_Brennic_CastOpen` keeps the Cast take's 47 frames and blends the arms
+  forward and out toward S1's pose. `RivalFigure` plays it under the non-flat looks.
+- No studio still was used: the concepts already existed.
+
+**Hands** (`apps/vr/art/hands/build_hands.py`). Built from an MPFB (MakeHuman, CC0) adult male with the game_engine rig.
+- Geometry: both forearms and hands, cut at 42 % of the forearm and subdivided once (28.6k tris), with a dark wool
+  sleeve over each forearm and leaf end bones.
+- Skin: regional colour in a fresh UV (tanned backs, pinker palms and tips, redder knuckles, nails from MPFB's mask).
+- `-run=CreatePlayerHands` builds `M_PlayerHandsEpic` (subsurface), `M_PlayerHandsLite` (the quest fallback) and
+  `M_PlayerSleeve`.
+- Posing: `PlayerHandsLook` places every bone at its HandFrame joint and turns it so its rest direction and the palm
+  normal map onto the live ones. Only joint positions enter, never a rotation convention.
+- In the S1 shot only, a one-handed pose gets its mirror, so both hands show as in S1.
+
+**Crowd and stand banners** (`apps/vr/art/crowd-painted/`).
+- Source: two studio stills (GPT Image 2.5, `crowd-standing.txt`, `crowd-seated.txt`) of ten colourful cheering Roman
+  spectators each, on chroma green.
+- Packing: `pack_crowd.py` keys them and finds figures by connected components. It packs five per T57 crowd variant at
+  that variant's card aspect, so every card keeps its size and only its atlas rect changes. It also hangs S1's red and
+  gold banner in a free column for T65's flat banner cards.
+- Runtime: `CrowdLook::Apply` re-points the cards, mirrors every other figure and jitters scale by up to 12 % about the
+  feet.
+- Studio stills used by Tier B: 2 of 40.
+
+## 3. Frame time (1376 x 768, `capture-epic.ps1`, the creature scene unless noted)
+
+| Round | GPU ms | Frame ms | What moved it |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| r0 | 11.1 | 12.0 | First deferred run: atmosphere, clouds, Lumen, VSM |
+| r1 | 7.2 | 8.2 | Painted sky dome in place of volumetric clouds |
+| r2 | 5.1 | 8.0 | (crowd, hands, Cast; no GPU growth) |
+| r3 | 5.3 | 8.2 | Fire heart, ward water |
+| r4 | 5.3 | 8.8 | Floor brazier fires, cuff |
+| r5 | 7.8 | 8.7 | Wall banners and coping, sky haze |
+| r6 | 7.8 | 8.8 | Gate, frozen S1 clock |
+
+The game thread, not the GPU, bounds the frame at about 8.5 ms (the -game editor build on emulated x64). Quest's D-G4 on
+the merged branch (`-MageArenaLook=quest`): draws median 134, p95 138 (limit 150); BasePass median 171k triangles. The
+skinned hands cost 2 draws and 28.6k triangles.
+
+## 4. The grade-LUT fit
+
+- Tool: `apps/vr/tools/look/fit_grade_lut.py`, BP's fitter (`kiro/bp scripts/lookdev/fit_grade_lut.py`) with S1 as the
+  default target.
+- Fit: the curve model at strength 0.8 on nine matched regions (`s1-grade-regions.json`: sand near and far, both walls,
+  sky, both crowd banks, foreground stone), fitted on the r2c frame.
+- Result: per-channel display gammas R 1.44, G 1.01, B 0.71 and a lift of 0.013. It pulls the orange excess out of sand,
+  stone and crowd and lifts the blues; the water stays turquoise and the fire orange.
+- Shipping: `T_EpicGradeLUT` (256 x 16) goes into the post volume's colour-grading LUT (`-MageArenaEpicNoLut` turns it
+  off).
+- Lesson: a per-channel curve cannot both brighten the sand and darken the walls, as S1 asks. That value separation is
+  lighting (which surfaces the sun reaches), not grade.
+
+## 5. Pitfalls
+
+- **Ward graph mismatch.** `M_EpicWard` began as a copy of `M_Q_Ward`. When Tier A moved the arch lift into the shader
+  (b826e92: upright cards, the wave lifted inside them by two more card floats), the old copy drew the cards as a
+  full-height wall of water that hid Brennic and the bolt. A material that copies another tier's graph must move with it.
+  It now carries the four-float arch graph (8e05c03).
+- **Alpha in colour comparisons.** The spell lights and the fire heart chose each layer's colour with
+  `FLinearColor::GetMax()`, which counts alpha. Black with alpha 1 already scored 1, so every glow fell back to the
+  default orange and the heart never found a warm core. A second bug compounded it: reading a parameter through the
+  `FMaterialParameterInfo` overload returned black on a MID; `FHashedMaterialParameterInfo(Name)` works. Compare RGB
+  only (`FMath::Max3`).
+- **MPFB thumb and the recorded clips.** The thumb hook was not the rig mapping. The clips curl the thumb: the ward clip's
+  distal phalanx turns about 130 degrees back on the one before it. For the picture only, each thumb segment is held
+  within 30 degrees of its parent; the gesture pipeline never sees it. The finger bones map onto OpenXR joints one to one
+  (MPFB `*_01` heads sit on the proximal joints); `thumb_01` is the metacarpal.
+- **Card bends.** Upright cards squared to a curve fan apart under the bend (dark wedges at the ward base). Widening them
+  overlaps translucency and shows seams. The fix was Tier A's: upright edge-to-edge cards with the lift in the shader.
+- Bounds of a posed skeletal mesh stay at the reference pose. The poseable hands were culled until their bounds scale
+  went to 20.
+- The FBX import carries a scale of 100 on the armature: component-space rest transforms have scale 100, so a posed bone
+  must keep its rest scale.
+- Changing an image's colour space in Blender after writing its pixels reloads the buffer as black. Set the colour space
+  first.
+- A Blender bake with margin 0 leaves edge texels black, which a rasterised coverage mask then counts as inside (dark
+  cracks along every UV seam). Bake with a margin.
+- Generated `TEXT()` HLSL written through shell heredocs lost its `\n` escapes. Patch C++ string literals from a script
+  file, not inline.
+
+## 6. Open items, ranked by visible gain
+
+1. Brennic's presence at 16 m. The face and hands are a few pixels: a heavier rim, a brighter cast glow on his face, or
+   a larger hand fire would read more than geometry.
+2. Brennic's MPFB hands (finger-separated) and a curly hair silhouette. They need a new skeletal asset (geometry, UVs,
+   skinning); skipped because the gain at 16 m is small.
+3. The cuff bars still sit over the left hand; a wrist-mounted cuff that follows the hand would read as part of the
+   costume.
+4. The panorama's hills barely show over the stands; a separate hill silhouette layer would read as S1's horizon.
+5. Crowd: two stills give 20 figures; more stills (and seated fronts for the near tiers) would hide the repeats.
+6. The epic grade is fitted once (r2c); a refit on the final frame (`fit_grade_lut.py`) would follow the later lighting.
