diff --git a/apps/vr/art/style/README.md b/apps/vr/art/style/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f665f0a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apps/vr/art/style/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Art style manifests
+
+One folder per art style (`-MageArenaStyle=<id>`, `Look/ArenaStyle.h`), each with a `style.json` that names what the style
+is made of. A retarget is a new folder plus regeneration through the same pipelines
+(`docs/concepts/RETARGET-CHALK-SLATE-2026-10-28.md` section 6).
+
+| Id | Status | Target |
+|---|---|---|
+| `painted` | Built (the graphics push, 2026-10-28) | Key art S1 (retired) |
+| `chalk` | Planned: slots described, no asset yet | S30-VR, style 30 Chalk & Slate |
+
+## Schema (`style.json`)
+
+| Key | Type | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | string | The `-MageArenaStyle` value. |
+| `title`, `status`, `target` | string | What the style is, whether its assets exist, the image it is judged against. |
+| `assetFolders` | object | Where the built assets and source PNGs live: `quest` and `spells` (Unreal package folders), `art` and `artSpells` (repo PNG folders). The commandlets and prep scripts take the style id and use these. |
+| `styleBlock` | string | The STYLE BLOCK every generated asset carries (name the process, not adjectives). |
+| `opposites` | string | What every prompt excludes. |
+| `suffixes` | object | Added after the subject by slot kind: `texture` (tileable, flat orthographic, even light), `figure` (full figure, readable silhouette), `vfx` (a sprite on a plain ground), `sky`. |
+| `palette` | object | Named colours, hex sRGB. |
+| `slots` | object | One entry a texture or figure to generate: `kind` (texture, figure, vfx, sky), `aspect` (1:1, 16:9, 9:16), `subject` (the slot's own sentence), `asset` (the asset it feeds), and for built styles `still` (the staged source). |
+| `material` | object | The shader parameters the style tunes, with starting values. |
+| `grade` | string | How the style's grade is done (in content, in post, none). |
+
+## Prompt composition
+
+`apps/vr/tools/keyart/studio-still.mts gen --style <id> --slot <slot> --out <png> [--dry]` composes
+`styleBlock + slot subject + suffixes[kind] + "Avoid: " + opposites`, uses the slot's aspect unless `--aspect` is given,
+and logs `style` and `slot` in `studio-log.jsonl`. `--dry` prints the composed prompt and spends nothing.
+The painted set was made before this schema with free prompts; its `slots` record the subjects actually used, and its
+`styleBlock` is the S1-derived wording those prompts shared.
