From a3328af14050881279938f2e97c4169c7d3de422 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:07:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 078/139] feat(look): chalk probe 4, pointing hand and
 fingertip sigil, line backdrop, stroke fire

Chalk style only. The S30 shot (shot composition, gameplay untouched): the
right hand's middle, ring and little fingers fold and the thumb tucks
(QuestLook::PointingPose on the mirrored frame), the water sigil sits at the
right index fingertip in world space every frame, a bold red chalk telegraph
ellipse lies on the sand under the bolt's path, and the shot looks down -20
degrees so both forearms enter from the bottom. Backdrop re-prompted as white
chalk line work on slate, its top rubbed into slate. The sand rubs into the
slate before the dais on a curve. The warm bolt core is masked by its stroke
pattern with only a small white-yellow heart. Brennic: lighter, more
saturated crimson, a strong pale rim and a pale chalk glow behind him.
Wardstone and post chalk brighter. D-G4 p95 118.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
