From b7f51907f09b67dfc763663db2da73b3e2ce83b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:04:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 080/139] feat(look): chalk round p6, stroke fireball, rising
 ward, sigil spiral, wardstone fix

Chalk style only. Wardstones: the runtime dump showed the chalk instance's
parameters applied (bright 3.4, span 0.1); the stone still is sRGB, so its
slate sampled ~0.045 linear and 3.4x left it near black. 10x with a tight
span draws white chalk line work on slate. Fire: a warm core draws only a
small hot heart (the sphere stays for the D-G4 census), the stroke shell
cards a third larger. Ward: a band thrown up from the left hand, sweeping
left and rising, upright cards. Sigil: bigger, a third ring and a spiral,
three drips under the fingertip; telegraph with a construction cross. Sand:
stroke-direction pastel still, paler, smudged into the slate toward the oval
rim as well as the dais.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
