From e3d28bcd8d18d620d7fcbafecd872f2ac8b94dc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:58:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 081/139] feat(art): Brennic in Chalk & Slate, drawn albedo,
 casting lunge, 1.15x

For the chalk style (-MageArenaStyle=chalk), on Brennic's own UVs (mesh, rig and the tracked
clips untouched):
- bake_chalk.py (generated by make_bake_chalk.py from bake_epic.py's bakes and masks plus
  chalk_synth.py) draws the albedo: each region in a shade, body and lit tone picked by the
  form light, a strong crimson wool robe, a dark cloak, a bronze collar and buckle, dark
  chalk contours where regions meet and along creases, hatching in the shade, the face
  (eyes, scowling brows, mouth) drawn bold over a near-black beard block so it reads at about
  40 px, chalk grain. -run=CreateBrennicEpic imports T_BrennicChalk_BaseColor and _ORM; the
  chalk figure material (Chalk/M_Q_Brennic) now prefers them with neutral tint and
  saturation, a stepped shade and a light contour (two lines in the quest asset builder).
- cast_lunge.py: A_Brennic_CastLunge (Cast's timing, 47 frames): a wide stance with the hips
  lowered, the torso leaning in, the right arm thrust toward the player and out to his side so
  it reads in silhouette, the left arm low and open. -run=ImportBrennicCastOpen -clip=CastLunge.
  RivalFigure plays it for Cast under chalk (CastOpen elsewhere). No cloth bones, so the
  robe does not flare.
- His visual scale is 1.15 under chalk (1.1 elsewhere); his bar rises with it. Visual only:
  hits and projectile targets come from the kernel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
