From f5c872074fa27f4e38f53512149ed87daeb1b5a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:12:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 083/139] feat(art): chalk-drawn hands and short slate-blue
 sleeves for Chalk & Slate

S30 shows bare, pastel-shaded forearms with dark sleeves only at the bottom edge:
- build_hands.py: the sleeve is a short cuff of cloth near the elbow (36-58 % of the forearm,
  over the skin's cut) instead of a tube to the wrist, for every look.
- chalk_hands.py (exec'd by build_hands.py, the same bakes and UV): T_PlayerHandsChalk_BaseColor,
  warm pastel skin drawn in pencil and chalk (creases across the finger joints, the main
  knuckles' outlines, veins on the backs of the hands and wrists, hatching in the shade,
  grain) and the sleeves in slate-blue cloth with chalk fold lines.
- -run=CreatePlayerHands imports it and builds M_PlayerSleeveChalk (unlit, two-step light);
  PlayerHandsLook puts it on the sleeves under the chalk style. The chalk skin material
  (Chalk/M_Q_Hands) prefers the drawn texture with neutral tint and a light contour (two
  lines in the quest asset builder).
- The commandlet now deletes SK_PlayerHands and its skeleton before importing: an FBX import
  over an existing skeletal mesh keeps that asset's old settings, and a reimport came in at
  a hundredth of the size (invisible in the shot).
The recorded pointing hand shows no artefact on this mesh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
