From 1958a74df4fb12180a6ae3e042ccec2f92afd1b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:21:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 084/139] feat(look): chalk bronze cuff with four runes and the
 wrist HUD drawn in

Under the chalk style the left wrist wears S30's bronze cuff (Look/ChalkCuffLook,
M_ChalkCuffHud built by -run=CreateCuffStyled), and the HUD that floated over the left hand
moves into it:
- the shader measures the angle round the wrist from the camera, so the four inlaid runes
  always sit on the side facing the eye; the first LitRunes are lit in coloured chalk (one
  per unlocked tier; two in the S30 shot), the rest engraved dark;
- under them four slim chalk tally strips in softened versions of the old bars' hues (HP
  magenta, mana blue, stamina green, clock gold), each filled to the same fraction the bars
  showed;
- the collar crack draws a warm-white seam across the band (its old seam sat on the panel).
SessionPresentation feeds the gauges and the crack and hides the panel and bars under
chalk only; the cue text, the gameplay and the other styles are unchanged. The hand
presentation poses this cuff and falls back to the plain chalk cuff when the asset is missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
