From aa0c826b149602d978368c1032e62e3d94306146 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:35:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 085/139] feat(art): Brennic reads drawn at 16 m, screen-width
 chalk contour, gold accents, lunge fire

Chalk & Slate, hero-4 (Brennic is about 40 px in the game camera):
- M_BrennicHull (-run=CreateBrennicEpic): an inverted hull whose push grows with distance,
  so its dark chalk contour stays about 2 px wide on screen, back faces only and broken
  like a stroke. RivalFigure adds it under chalk, led by the figure (one draw), tagged
  ChalkHull so the look's material pass skips it; the figure's visibility now propagates.
- The drawn albedo keeps value blocks that survive the low mips: a paler face plane, a
  near-black beard and brows, the robe's lit and shade split pushed apart, wider region
  contours, and the belt and bracers in gold with the collar and brooch (shins and sandals
  stay brown).
- The lunge's fire: under chalk his right (thrusting) hand burns large and the left only as
  an ember. The S30 shot logs MAGEVR_RIVAL_HAND (the hand's world position and clip time)
  for the bolt's placement.

