From 26aecf1f3bf127f749d72409c84144c7d2eca9c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:46:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 091/139] feat(look): chalk round p9, full-screen chalk pass,
 big thrown bolt, slate wardstones

Under -MageArenaStyle=chalk only (flat and painted unchanged); the S30 shot staging is shot-only.
- M_Q_ChalkPost: one blendable post-process material on the camera (after tonemapping): five depth
  taps (cross Laplacian + silhouette) drawn as broken strokes, light on slate and dark on sand and
  skin; one shared 1 px chalk/paper grain; a soft luminance posterize (6 steps at 0.35); a smudged
  slate vignette at the bottom and sides. -MageArenaChalkPost=0 drops it. It needs the post pass:
  with MobileHDR off it is absent.
- Cost (D-G4 stress, 1920x1080 offscreen, desktop GPU): ES3.1 mobile proxy, MobileHDR on, GPU
  median 2.44 ms with vs 1.72 without (+0.72); SM5 3.13 vs 2.92 (+0.21); +1 draw.
- S30 bolt: thrown from his thrust hand (hero-5 pose, 367.6, -45.2, 140.1 cm), mid-air on the line
  to the player at p7's distance (BoltOutM 3.2 from the seat) and size.
- Telegraph ring beside the bolt (3.8 m in front of him, 1.7 m right), brighter, never hidden.
- Wardstones: slate with a few chalk lines (bright 1.4, floor 0.04), not white bricks.

D-G4 chalk with Tier B hero-5 and the pass: draws median 113, p95 115; BasePass 195k.

