From 2a1e5156bd1e128069873325d213a231d06ad18e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:12:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 094/139] feat(look): chalk round p10, near-field-safe chalk
 pass, oval sand, left ward curtain

Under -MageArenaStyle=chalk only (flat and painted unchanged).
- Chalk pass: no depth edges and no banding within 1.5 m of the eye (the judges' white halos round
  the hands), grain halved (0.08), a third of it near the eye, none on hot emissive; posterize
  0.2; the vignette spares the near field (it dimmed the cuff).
- Cost on the true ES3.1 path, MobileHDR on (D-G4 stress, 1920x1080, desktop GPU): GPU median
  2.34 ms with vs 1.99 without (+0.35), p95 3.00 vs 2.51, +1 draw. p9's 9.25 ms p95 was a
  first-launch phase (~35 s at ~7 ms after the material was rebuilt), not the steady pass.
- Sand: rubs out into the slate on a drawn ellipse short of the dais (EdgeX -720, EdgeCurve
  0.0005, EdgeSpan 200), curving away to both sides; no straight sand/dais line.
- Ward: under chalk the cards on the left of the arc stand up to 2.3x as tall (a streaky curtain
  from the left hand), Veil 0.72 makes it translucent; the footprint is unchanged.
- Wardstones: mid-value grey chalk blocks with white edges (bright 3).

D-G4 chalk with Tier B hero-6 and the pass: draws median 112, p95 115; BasePass 196k.
Suite 346/349 (Fire.Golden, Overlay.Golden, Rivals.NullPath).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
