From 11eb2b3f7d54f6f38b5c4efcaa99f7edf2499c2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:42:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 098/139] feat(look): chalk round p11, full sand bowl, charcoal
 ground, one ward sweep, drawn wardstones

Under -MageArenaStyle=chalk only (flat and painted unchanged); the S30 shot staging is shot-only.
- Sand fills the floor toward the seat again: a soft 3.8 m rub-out from the dais front, a wider rim
  fade (0.32), drawn footprints and scuffs (Scuff), no blob mask.
- Ground: slate lifted toward S30's blue-grey charcoal, rubbed chalk dust and soft wipes on the
  board and the sand's rub-out (Dust); construction guides and rune lines broken into chalk.
- Ward (chalk): one continuous curtain, no printed wave: procedural streaky translucent chalk water
  on p9's lifted sweep, rising 1.6 wave heights higher toward the left hand (cards twice as tall).
- Fire: denser stroke cards, a bigger ragged bright core in warm yellow-white.
- Telegraph ring directly under the bolt's path, 2.5 m behind it toward him.
- Wardstones: 2D chalk-drawn obelisk cards (the pylon still, alpha-cut, T_Q_ChalkObelisk,
  M_Q_ChalkWardstone) facing the seat, the violet Tithe flame on top; T_Q_ChalkPylon and the
  UseMeshUv surface param are gone.
- Chalk figure rim aimed from above and behind toward the camera with a floor, so Brennic's left
  side catches it too (Tier B's request).
- Chalk pass vignette slate in display space (#2A2F33).

D-G4 chalk with Tier B hero-7 and the pass: draws median 107, p95 109; BasePass 167k.
Suite 346/349 (Fire.Golden, Overlay.Golden, Rivals.NullPath).

