From 8f8302021dc481cbfa305d45af59bd4207946173 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:40:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 108/139] feat(look): 2.5D s3, dark-slate chalk panorama with a
 painted floor, water flipbook ward

Behind -MageArena25D=1 under chalk; the p11 look stays the default.
- Panorama redone as white chalk line work on near-black slate (the judges: s2 read as a grey
  engraving): ControlNet depth 0.75 / edges 0.4, scene prompt in gen/static-scene/s3/; faces front
  s71, left s91, right s93 and a new floor face (pitch -80, floor-only prompt, s83), stitched to
  yaw +-145, pitch +35..-90 (-MageArena25DPitch= on the export).
- Depth gate soft and filtered (bilinear, block max instead of min): the s2 sand mosaic was the
  p11 fallback showing through a stepped gate; the p11 specks fade where they would alias.
- Ward under 25D: M_Q_Ward25D, the chalk curtain carrying Tier B's water flipbook; the curtain's
  lower edge fades out.
- The rival's greybox HP bar is not drawn over the painted figure under 25D.
- A flipbook bolt's old core sphere shrinks to a point instead of hiding (the D-G4 census counts it).

D-G4 chalk with the flag: desktop draws median 102, p95 104, BasePass 116k; ES3.1 proxy draws 79,
GPU median 4.43 ms vs 4.39 without the flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
