From bef2c5ac1762413f4cb128b2500c696bd4c92072 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:29:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 114/139] feat(look): 2.5D s4, s2's raked sand in s3's chalk
 scene, lighter blue ward, cleanups

Behind -MageArena25D=1 under chalk; the p11 look stays the default.
- Sand: stitch_25d.py --sand-face composites s2's ControlNet faces (muted ochre, raked strokes)
  into the s3 panorama under a soft sand mask, graded (--sand-gain 1.0 0.95 0.76) so it reaches the
  screen near S30's ochre (measured 200,177,151 against 203,173,136); no blob stamps.
- Ward (chalk curtain and its 25D water): chalk-blue, Veil 0.38, the flipbook's coverage halved.
- Rune rings antialiased by their own screen derivative (fwidth), not fixed widths.
- Under 25D: the wardstone cap orbs shrink to a point (the violet chalk flame stays the Tithe
  signal); the shot's sigil drips are not made.
- A soft chalk shadow pool under the painted Brennic card.

D-G4 with the flag: desktop draws median 103 / p95 105, BasePass 120k; ES3.1 draws 80, GPU median
4.48 ms. Suite 346/350: the three known reds plus Sigils.Accuracy on its 0.5 ms p95 timing bound
only (Tier B's Flux/H3 jobs on the GPU).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
