From 3acea0ad04bac1dc05c89d6dd1d6ba9d712d295b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:13:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 120/139] fix(art): hand hatching follows the form, no wood
 grain

Judges still saw a wood-grain contour pattern on the thumb and the right
hand: hero-7's pencil hatching was drawn in UV space, so on a finger its
stripes closed into rings. chalk_hands.py (HANDS_HATCH3D=1) now draws the
fine hatch and a cross-hatch from each texel's 3D position, in planar
sections whose normals lie across the hand's long axis, so the strokes run
along the hand and fingers; coarser (3.5 mm), lower contrast (0.3 / 0.22),
soft-edged, only on the shade side. The drawn base is rebuilt with it (the
UVs and painted albedo come out byte-identical), and hands_paint.py lines
mode folds the painted anatomy in at gain 0.6. Re-run -run=CreatePlayerHands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
