From cd3276af4bf58b1a0a718a87e3a130542dd39ec1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:46:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 121/139] feat(art): Brennic pages at 512 px cells, one matte
 and chalk pass for every clip

Judges at 4 m: soft and upscaled, arms crushed to black, a dark speckled
fringe on the H3 clips against a cream sticker edge on the others, and the
figure growing mid-clip. pack_pages.py re-exports every duel clip (Idle,
Cast, Hit, Death, Ward, Strafe, Sunfall) from the 768 px sources into 512 px
cells, 8 x 8 on 4096 px pages (T_RivalSprite_P0..P4, 304 cells), each clip
through the same pass: matte holes filled, specks dropped, edge pulled in and
decontaminated; standing clips scaled about the feet to the idle's
feet-to-head height (growth only), crouching ones to its head width; colour
matched to the idle; deep shadow lifted so thin limbs keep their colour; a
pastel posterize, a charcoal contour capped at a third of the local
thickness, and a thin, broken, grainy chalk edge instead of the cream line.
The 256 px pages (T_RivalSprite, T_RivalSprite2) are retired.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
