From 0002fd5196fb847cf3041a67a176cb5002cb8f7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 06:46:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 122/139] feat(look): Brennic flipbook on multi-page 512 px
 cells with a depth card

RivalSprite now reads clips from 8 x 8 cells on 4096 px pages (a clip on
one page, its own rate; Death at 18 fps) and draws them on a 32 x 32 grid
card (SM_RivalCardGrid, card_grid.py): the depth page of each colour page
(T_RivalSprite_D<n>, the matte's inflated silhouette, 128 px cells) pushes
the grid toward the seat in the vertex shader, DepthCm 28 at 1x
(-MageArenaSpriteDepthCm= to try others, -MageArenaSpriteDepth=0 for the
flat card). Same one draw, 2,048 triangles, one vertex texture fetch. Only
the three pages the wired clips use load. SpriteFrameAt covers pages and
per-clip rates. Re-run -run=CreateRivalSprite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
