From d01c7a114e0245022567a90aa070e51153c2c08a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:39:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 124/139] feat(look): 2.5D s5b, water-sheet ward, translucent
 chalk fire, sand lifted

Behind -MageArena25D=1 under chalk; the p11 look stays the default.
- Ward curtain: a sheet of chalk water, not rain: dense broken strokes of varied width that
  curl, finer strands between them, a low chalk-blue wash (0.28 x Veil 0.55, about 0.15), a crest
  band of foam dashes instead of one thin line, droplets under it.
- M_Q_FireChalk is translucent (additive washed out to pale peach on the lit sand): its warm
  pastel bands cover the sand, with dark-red broken strokes at the band edges, a ragged rim and
  a hot core.
- Sand composite lifted to s4b's ochre on screen (--sand-gain 1.2 1.16 0.95; measured 203,178,152).

Built with Tier B round 5 (dc4fb68 419e624 f504bf1 5d02be5 as 3acea0a cd3276a 0002fd5 2f91e28).
D-G4 with the flag: desktop draws median 102 / p95 104, BasePass 117k; ES3.1 79 draws, GPU
median 4.46 ms. Suite 346/350: the three known reds plus Sigils.Accuracy on its 0.5 ms p95
timing bound only (0.54 ms, Tier B's Flux jobs on the GPU).

