From 681abaa70bdcb06c0781ffe09b98d3515bd640de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:28:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 125/139] feat(look): 2.5D s6, chalk-on-dark hands, cuff and
 sleeve, sand edge, scribbled fire core

Behind -MageArena25D=1 under chalk for the shot staging and the panorama; the hand, cuff and sleeve
materials change under chalk for every look that uses them.
- Hands (M_Q_Hands, the chalk figure shader): a broken, jittered, variable-width light chalk
  contour band at the silhouette (fresnel, ChalkLine) and soft pastel highlight patches over the
  hatching (Pastel); in the material, so the post pass keeps out of the near field.
- Cuff (CreateCuffStyled, M_ChalkCuffHud): pale chalk rubbed over the bronze in soft patches,
  broken chalk-white strokes along both lips, unlit runes drawn in chalk, lit runes keep their
  glow; metallic 0.25, roughness 0.75. Sleeve (CreatePlayerHands, M_PlayerSleeveChalk): a broken
  light chalk stroke along its silhouette and soft grain. Binaries rebuilt by both commandlets.
- Sand edge (stitch_25d.py): the boundary rubbed out irregularly into the slate (low-frequency
  noise), a smeared pastel border and stray sand grains on the slate.
- Floor rings: uneven pressure, breaks, chalk-dust halos and eraser smears (--rings).
- Fire core: white-yellow chalk scribbles instead of a flat disc.
- The S30 shot's bolt moves toward his thrusting hand's side nearer than 10 m (0.7 m at 4 m);
  the telegraph ring's strokes are brighter.

D-G4 with the flag: desktop draws median 101 / p95 103, BasePass 118k; ES3.1 79 draws, GPU
median 1.73 ms (box idle). Suite 347/350 (Fire.Golden, Overlay.Golden, Rivals.NullPath).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
