From 6470adfb371f943ce336b6d871660c28c532927e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:03:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 126/139] feat(look): 2.5D s7, sweeping ward strokes, detailed
 near slate, drawn footprints, chalk sigil

Behind -MageArena25D=1 under chalk; the p11 look stays the default.
- Ward curtain: fewer, wider sweeping chalk-blue strokes slanting with the sheet (36 columns,
  broken in longer segments), the foam-dash crest kept, the busy thin squiggles almost gone; the
  curtain fades out at its cards' lower edge, so no dark half-disc on the slate under it.
- Near slate: the projection adds world-space chalk dust, soft erasure smudges and scuffs on
  floor faces within about 10 m of the eye where the painting is slate (Detail).
- Sand (stitch_25d.py): dark footprint blobs become shallow impressions with a broken pale chalk
  rim, a fine directional pastel grain, and the elliptical edge dissolves further.
- Sigil: the shot's card takes Sketch (a rougher chalk ring) and a soft glow (Glow, M_Q_ChalkRune).

D-G4 with the flag: desktop draws median 102 / p95 104 (one 829 spike frame), BasePass 118k;
ES3.1 79 draws, GPU median 3.71 ms. Suite 346/350: the three known reds plus Sigils.Accuracy
on its 0.5 ms p95 timing bound only (0.96 ms, Tier B's ComfyUI batch on the GPU).

