From 0f6e2e42d8e2f299a90647b6d256399344c4fd6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:44:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 131/139] feat(art): Brennic re-rendered with a mantle-only
 cape, a real flinch and a sidestep

S5 judges: a dark halo, painted shading, the cape popping in and out, Hit
reading as a gesture, Strafe one small step, a rigid sail in Death and a
scale pop. Six pages of 512 px cells now (Idle 55, Cast 38, Hit 21, Death
50 at 14 fps, Ward 49, Strafe 64, Sunfall 43), all through the new chalk
pass (pale wobbly chalk contour, hatched pastel shading, no dark line):
new keys say the cloak is a short shoulder mantle with nothing hanging, to
match the idle every segment starts and ends on; Hit is a flinch (head
back, torso recoil, a step back) and recovery; Strafe is a step out, a
crossing shuffle and a step back (loops); Death falls to a lying key
inpainted with the mantle on his back; Cast is re-rendered by LTX from a
new lunge key. The pack's scale is measured per pose (standing height, head
width, or lying length against the idle) and interpolated, so nothing holds
and pops; the rig bound is wider so the cast hand is not cut to a stump.
Re-run -run=CreateRivalSprite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
